TOOLING REQUIREMENT

This repository has a prebuilt Repowise index available to you over MCP. It is
the fastest way to find the code this task touches, and you are expected to use
it rather than searching the tree blind.

Before you edit any file, you MUST use the Repowise tools to locate the code you
need to change. Use them again whenever you are unsure where something lives or
how it is wired. Do not skip this step, and do not fall back to grepping the
tree until the Repowise tools have failed to answer.

| tool | when to call it |
|------|-----------------|
| `get_answer(question)` | First call for any how / where / why question about this codebase. |
| `search_codebase(query)` | Find code by concept, symbol, or path when you do not yet know what to open. |
| `get_context(targets=[...])` | Triage a file, module, or symbol before you edit it: docs, signatures, callers. |
| `get_symbol(id)` | Fetch one verified symbol body for an id an earlier response named. A follow-up, not an entry point. |

These tools decide WHICH files matter. They do not replace opening the files you
are about to change: read the code you edit, and check the tests that cover it.
